# Leave VITE_API_URL unset (commented out) so the app auto-detects its backend
# from the current browser origin, using the same build for every environment:
#   - localhost / 127.0.0.1        -> http://localhost:3001/api
#   - crm.espainternational.co.in  -> https://crm.espainternational.co.in/api  (dev server)
#   - espacrm.in                   -> https://espacrm.in/api                  (production)
#
# Only uncomment VITE_API_URL to force a single fixed backend for every environment,
# e.g. when tunneling your local backend through ngrok so an external service
# (WhatsApp/TeleCMI webhooks) can reach it:
# VITE_API_URL=https://your-ngrok-url.ngrok-free.dev
